      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Abdominal apoplexy is an uncommon disorder typically due to atheromatous vascular disease, inflammatory processes such as pancreatitis eroding into large blood vessels or vasculitis. We describe an unusual case due to unrecognised syphilis masquerading as pancreatitis."},
